Render delegate with a host CameraUtilFraming whose display window differs from its data window

see #2819

A red sphere is rendered by the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate, driven like a Hydra host (e.g. maya-hydra) in a
160x120 render buffer. The host sends a framing whose display window positions the film in the buffer and whose data
window is the part of the buffer to fill: film translate, overscan, zoom and a render region. The host's buffer must
not be resized, and the sphere must be where CameraUtilFraming::ApplyToProjectionMatrix puts it, the pixels outside of
the data window being left cleared. A host without a framing (display window equal to the data window) must render as
before, also after the framing was used. The camera aperture offset is then set and reset, the image must come back.
The scenario only runs with the render delegate, see testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked
in test.cpp, and the last one is compared against the reference image.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
